  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "This plate turns for a reason. It helps food heat more evenly. A magnetron inside the oven generates microwaves. The metal walls guide and reflect them around the cavity. Water molecules have uneven electrical charge, so they behave like tiny dipoles. The changing field makes them rotate back and forth. Their motion spreads energy to nearby molecules as heat. The oven can have hotter and cooler regions. The turntable moves food through those regions for more even heating. The microwaves do not make the food radioactive. Once the oven stops, the field is gone, but the heat remains. Microwave energy becomes molecular motion and molecular motion becomes heat.",
